{#
  A post's attached media (1 to 4) — module spec layout: 1 wide, 2 side
  by side, 3 with one tall on the left, 4 in a 2x2 (public/assets/css/
  components.css' .groups-media-grid-{count} rules). `media` is a
  Modules\Gallery\Api\DelegatedMedia[], already in attachment order.

  Each cell stays a REAL <a> to the media's own large/original rendition,
  so with no JS it opens in a new tab exactly as it always did. On top of
  that it carries `.gallery-lightbox-trigger` and the medium/large data
  attributes gallery.js's own lightbox reads, so a click opens the
  in-page viewer with prev/next across this post's photos instead —
  groups hard-requires gallery (module.json's `requires`), so reusing its
  lightbox is reusing a dependency this module already has rather than
  writing a second one that would drift.

  gallery.js binds its trigger click WITHOUT preventDefault, so the <a>'s
  own navigation has to be stopped somewhere: groups.js does it, and only
  when the lightbox is genuinely present and the cell has a rendition to
  show. That keeps the no-JS/failed-processing paths on the plain link.

  `data-media-id`/`data-status` are read by groups.js: a cell still
  'pending'/'processing' gets polled (GET /groups/{id}/media-status)
  until the background resize (Task\ProcessPhotoHandler/
  ProcessVideoHandler) finishes, then swapped in place for the real
  thumbnail with no page reload.
#}
{% if media is not empty %}
    {% set media_count = media|length %}
    <div class="groups-media-grid groups-media-grid-{{ media_count }} mt-2">
        {% for m in media %}
            {# How wide this cell actually draws, as a share of the grid —
               the `sizes` hint media_thumb.html.twig needs to pick between
               the two renditions it offers (issue #330). The shares mirror
               components.css' own .groups-media-grid-{count} rules: one
               media fills the grid, two and four take half of it, and three
               is a 2fr cell beside two 1fr ones. The grid itself is the
               feed's width below 992px and is capped at 420px above it. #}
            {% set cell_share = media_count == 1
                ? 1
                : (media_count == 3 ? (loop.first ? 0.67 : 0.33) : 0.5) %}
            {% set cell_sizes = '(min-width: 992px) ' ~ (420 * cell_share)|round ~ 'px, ' ~ (100 * cell_share)|round ~ 'vw' %}
            <a href="/gallery/media/{{ m.id }}/{{ m.mediaType == 'video' ? 'original' : 'large' }}"
               target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="groups-media-cell text-decoration-none gallery-lightbox-trigger"
               data-media-id="{{ m.id }}" data-status="{{ m.processingStatus }}"
               data-type="{{ m.mediaType }}"
               {# Same `sizes` the <img> below carries, kept on the cell so
                  groups.js can repeat it on the thumbnail it builds when a
                  still-processing media finishes — the two renders of the
                  same cell must not disagree about how wide it is. #}
               data-thumb-sizes="{{ cell_sizes }}"
               {# Only a finished media has renditions to show; gallery.js
                  skips a trigger with no data-medium-url and marks it
                  aria-disabled, which is exactly right for one still
                  processing or failed. #}
               {% if m.processingStatus == 'done' %}
                   data-medium-url="/gallery/media/{{ m.id }}/medium"
                   data-large-url="/gallery/media/{{ m.id }}/{{ m.mediaType == 'video' ? 'original' : 'large' }}"
                   {# The lightbox's own download button — the gallery's route,
                      which names the file the way the album's zip does
                      (Modules\Gallery\Service\MediaFileName) and re-checks
                      this group's access on its own. #}
                   data-download-url="/gallery/media/{{ m.id }}/download"
               {% endif %}>
                {% include '@groups/partials/media_thumb.html.twig' with { media: m, sizes: cell_sizes } %}
            </a>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
